# Filename : start.config
# Description:
#     Establish the names of lab containers and some of their properties, including:
#       User names
#       Network connections
#       lab master seed
#
# Refer to the "Labtainer Lab Designer User Guide" for details.
#
# slow-scan topology: one flat LAN, three hosts.
#
#   attacker 172.20.0.10   runs scan.py / nmap
#   client   172.20.0.20   generates benign traffic
#   victim   172.20.0.30   services (22, 80, 8081, 9090) + monitor + detectors
#
# All hosts share one L2 segment, so no router and no static routes are needed.
# NOTE: labs/denyhost and labs/httplab also use 172.20.0.0/24; stop them first.

GLOBAL_SETTINGS

	# LAB_MASTER_SEED - this is the master seed string specific to this laboratory
	LAB_MASTER_SEED slow-scan_2736403_master_seed

# SUBNETS
# GATEWAY is Docker's link to the host: it must be inside MASK and must not be
# a container address.
# The network name becomes the Docker network name (lower-cased). Several other
# labs use a network called LAN on different subnets; a unique name keeps a
# leftover network from one of them from hijacking ours.
NETWORK SLOWSCAN_LAN
	MASK 172.20.0.0/24
	GATEWAY 172.20.0.100

# CONTAINERS
CONTAINER attacker
	USER ubuntu
	TERMINALS 1
	SLOWSCAN_LAN 172.20.0.10

CONTAINER client
	USER ubuntu
	TERMINALS 1
	SLOWSCAN_LAN 172.20.0.20

CONTAINER victim
	USER ubuntu
	TERMINALS 1
	SLOWSCAN_LAN 172.20.0.30
